# Build context for the API image (Dockerfile, docs/container.md).
#
# Allowlist: everything is excluded, then only the files the API build reads are let back in. A file
# added anywhere else in the repository (a local .env, a key, a dump, an APK, scratch output) can
# never reach the build context by accident.
*

!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!.npmrc
!tsconfig.base.json
!packages/contracts/package.json
!packages/contracts/tsconfig.json
!packages/contracts/tsconfig.build.json
!packages/contracts/src/
!apps/api/package.json
!apps/api/tsconfig.json
!apps/api/tsconfig.build.json
!apps/api/src/
!apps/web/package.json
!deploy/container/certs/rds-eu-west-1-bundle.pem
!deploy/container/certs/SHA256SUMS

# Defence in depth: even inside the allowed directories, never send secrets, local state or output.
**/.git
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/*service-account*.json
**/*-credentials.json
**/google-services.json
**/.netrc
**/*.tfstate*
**/*.rdb
**/*.sqlite*
**/*.db
**/*.dump
**/*.sql.gz
**/*.apk
**/*.aab
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.data
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/screenshots
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.claude
**/.pnpm-store

# The one certificate file the image needs (public RDS CA roots), re-allowed after the *.pem rule.
!deploy/container/certs/rds-eu-west-1-bundle.pem
